# The circle tour: one full CCW circle, driven as an arc twist (v = omega*r).
#
# PLAYFIELD SIZING (2026-08-14). The original radius was 250 mm, which does
# not fit: driven CCW from the field centre the circle's centre sits at
# y = +250 and its top reaches y = +500 mm, against a 386 mm limit for the
# robot centre. Measured on hardware -- the run drove the robot to
# (182, 376) mm and the next tour then failed against the north rail.
#
# r = 150 mm puts the top of the circle at y = +300 mm, ~85 mm inside the
# limit, which exceeds the measured closure error so a normal run stays clear.
# 150 mm/s at 57.3 deg/s -> r = 150 mm; a full turn is 360 deg.

MARK circle
TWIST vx=150 omega=57.3 angle=360 timeout=30
STOP dwell=0.5

CAMFIX x=0 y=0 radius=150
